{"timestamp": 1783621546.592303, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I reported Bob\u2019s body in medbay. My route was weapons -> security -> electrical -> cafeteria -> medbay.\n\nEarly on I was in weapons, and Eve entered weapons from security around tick 4. I did not see a body in weapons at that time. Then I went to security and saw Charlie enter from navigation around tick 6, and Charlie was still in security through ticks 7-8. Later around tick 11 I saw Charlie moving around electrical/cafeteria area \u2014 looked like electrical toward cafeteria timing-wise.\n\nI didn\u2019t see Diana this round. I only found Bob in medbay; I didn\u2019t see Frank\u2019s body myself. If Frank was in weapons, Eve was the only person I saw near weapons, but that was early, so I\u2019m not hard accusing yet."}}
{"timestamp": 1783621559.4758, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My route was navigation -> security -> electrical -> cafeteria -> oxygen.\n\nI can confirm part of Alice\u2019s story: I came into security from navigation around tick 6, and Alice was there with me through tick 7. I saw Alice leave security toward electrical at tick 8, and I later saw Alice again in electrical around tick 11. So that lines up with what she said.\n\nI didn\u2019t see Bob or Frank at all this round, and I didn\u2019t see any bodies myself. The only other thing I saw was Eve leaving oxygen toward upper_engine at tick 15. I never saw Diana.\n\nSo from my POV, Alice\u2019s timing around security/electrical checks out. Eve was the only person I saw later, moving out of oxygen toward upper_engine, which might matter depending on when Bob died in medbay or where Frank\u2019s body was. I\u2019d like to hear from Diana and Eve before deciding."}}
{"timestamp": 1783621582.619796, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "My route was security -> weapons -> cafeteria -> oxygen. I was in weapons early, around the time Alice mentioned, but I saw no body there and I didn\u2019t see Frank or Bob at all.\n\nThe only player I actually saw this round was Charlie at tick 15 in oxygen \u2014 my notes are that Charlie entered oxygen from cafeteria. So I need to push back on Charlie saying he saw me leaving oxygen toward upper_engine at tick 15. I did not go to upper_engine; I was in oxygen when Charlie came in.\n\nThat contradiction makes me suspicious of Charlie, especially because Alice and Charlie are mostly confirming each other, but Charlie\u2019s detail about me doesn\u2019t match what I saw. I still want to hear Diana, but right now Charlie\u2019s story has the biggest issue to me."}}
{"timestamp": 1783621602.793921, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I was mostly on the left/mid side. My route was electrical -> medbay briefly -> storage -> back through medbay/electrical -> cafeteria -> weapons/security area.\n\nImportant thing: I saw Bob enter medbay from upper engine around tick 7. He was alive then. I did not stay there long \u2014 I moved off after that, so I don\u2019t know when he died.\n\nFor Frank, I saw him leave electrical toward security around tick 9, and later I saw him go from security into weapons around tick 14. So Frank was alive pretty late, which makes the \u201cEve was in weapons early\u201d point feel less useful to me. If Frank died in/near weapons, it probably happened after tick 14.\n\nThe biggest weird thing to me is still Charlie and Eve disagreeing about oxygen at tick 15. Alice and Charlie matching early doesn\u2019t clear Charlie for the late kills, especially if Frank was alive at tick 14. I\u2019m leaning that the Charlie/Eve contradiction is where we should focus, and Charlie\u2019s version sounded more specific but it\u2019s also the part being directly disputed."}}
{"timestamp": 1783621626.143252, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I want to add after hearing everyone: my report was definitely Bob in medbay. I never saw Frank\u2019s body, so Diana\u2019s info that Frank was alive around tick 14 going into weapons is important.\n\nCharlie and I only clear each other for the early security/electrical part \u2014 that does **not** clear him for the whole round. But I also don\u2019t think the Charlie/Eve oxygen contradiction alone is enough, because it could be timing or one of them misreading movement.\n\nThe thing that stands out most to me now is Diana\u2019s route and info: Diana says she saw Bob alive in/near medbay around tick 7, and also saw Frank alive going security to weapons around tick 14. That puts Diana near both victims\u2019 last known locations, including Frank very late. So I\u2019m actually more suspicious of Diana than I was at first.\n\nMy current lean is Diana for opportunity on both kills, but I\u2019m listening if anyone has a stronger reason to pick between Charlie and Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1783621640.380335, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I stand by my oxygen note: from my view at tick 15, I saw Eve leaving oxygen toward upper_engine as I came in from cafeteria. If Eve says she was still in oxygen, then either one of us misread timing/position, or that\u2019s a real contradiction \u2014 but I don\u2019t think that alone should decide the vote.\n\nLooking at both bodies, Diana worries me more now. She places herself near medbay when Bob was last alive, then says she saw Frank go into weapons very late around tick 14 while she was in that weapons/security area. That\u2019s proximity to both victims at important times. Alice\u2019s route is pretty consistent with what I saw, and Eve being in weapons early doesn\u2019t matter much if Frank was alive until tick 14.\n\nSo my lean is Diana. I\u2019m not cleared for the whole round, sure, but Diana\u2019s own info gives her the best opportunity for both kills."}}
{"timestamp": 1783621673.047413, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I\u2019ll restate my side clearly: my route was security -> weapons -> cafeteria -> oxygen. I never saw Bob or Frank, and I was in weapons early only \u2014 before Diana says Frank was alive going into weapons around tick 14, so that early weapons point should not be used against me.\n\nOn the oxygen thing: Charlie, I still think your tick 15 detail is wrong. I saw you enter oxygen from cafeteria; I did **not** leave toward upper engine. That contradiction bothers me, but I agree it may not be enough by itself.\n\nLooking at both deaths, Diana has the most opportunity by her own route: she was around medbay when Bob was last seen alive, and she was also around security/weapons when Frank was last seen alive very late. That\u2019s stronger than the oxygen disagreement right now.\n\nSo unless Diana has a really good explanation, I\u2019m leaning Diana for this vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1783621696.6016269, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I get why my route looks bad, but I want to be clear: I\u2019m the one giving the info that makes the timing tighter. If I were trying to hide opportunity, I would not volunteer that Bob was alive in medbay or that Frank was alive going into weapons late.\n\nBob: I saw him enter medbay at tick 7, and I left. Alice is the one who later ends in medbay and reports Bob. I\u2019m not saying that\u2019s definitely a self-report, but the reporter being the only person confirmed at Bob\u2019s body should not be ignored.\n\nFrank: I saw Frank alive very late \u2014 security to weapons around tick 14, and I also saw him in weapons around tick 15. That means early weapons stuff does not matter. If Frank died after that, then the key is who could access weapons around that timing. Charlie and Eve\u2019s oxygen story still has a direct contradiction at the exact late timing, and now everyone is kind of handwaving it because it\u2019s convenient to pile on me.\n\nCharlie is the one with a disputed late-game movement detail, and he and Alice are basically clearing each other early then steering the vote onto me. I think that\u2019s more suspicious than me openly sharing last-seen info. My vote lean is Charlie, not because Eve is clear, but because Charlie\u2019s late detail is the thing that doesn\u2019t match."}}
